Given an ellipse $C: \frac{x^{2}}{a^{2}}+ \frac{y^{2}}{b^{2}}=1 (a > b > 0)$ with left and right foci $F_{1}$ and $F_{2}$, respectively, and an eccentricity of $\frac{1}{2}$. There is a point $M(-3,0)$ such that $\overrightarrow{MF_{2}}=2 \overrightarrow{MF_{1}}$.
