If the values of two unknowns in a system of two linear equations are opposite to each other, we call this system of equations a "related system of equations."  
$(1)$ Determine whether the system of equations $\left\{\begin{array}{l}{3x-y=4}\\{x-3y=4}\end{array}\right.$ is a "related system of equations," and explain the reason;  
$(2)$ If the system of equations $\left\{\begin{array}{l}{x+3y=4-a}\\{x-y=3a}\end{array}\right.$ concerning $x$ and $y$ is a "related system of equations," find the value of $a$.

