Given the parametric equation of line $l$ as $\begin{cases}x=m+ \frac{ \sqrt{2}}{2}t \\ y= \frac{ \sqrt{2}}{2}t\end{cases} (t$ is the parameter), with the origin as the pole and the positive half-axis of $x$ as the polar axis to establish the polar coordinate system, the polar equation of ellipse $C$ is $\rho^2\cos^2\theta+3\rho^2\sin^2\theta=12$, and its left focus $F$ is on line $l$.

$(1)$ If line $l$ intersects ellipse $C$ at points $A$ and $B$, find the value of $|FA|\cdot|FB|$;

$(2)$ Find the maximum perimeter of the inscribed rectangle of ellipse $C$.

Given that the sum of the first $n$ terms of a sequence $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$ is $S_{n}=\dfrac{3n^{2}-n}{2}$.
(1) Find the general formula for $\left\{a_{n}\right\}$;
(2) Let $b_{n}=\dfrac{1}{a_{n}a_{n+1}}$, and the sum of the first $n$ terms of the sequence $\left\{b_{n}\right\}$ is $T_{n}$. If $t\leqslant 4T_{n}$ holds for all $n\in N^{*}$, find the maximum value of the real number $t$.

Given the function $y=f(x)$, if for any $x \in \mathbb{R}$, the equation $f(2x)=2f(x)$ always holds, then the function $y=f(x)$ is said to have property $P$.

$(1)$ If the function $y=f(x)$ has property $P$, and $f(4)=8$, then $f(1)=$\_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_;

$(2)$ If the function $y=f(x)$ has property $P$, and its expression on $(1,2]$ is $y=\cos x$, then $y=f(x)$ has exactly \_\_\_\_\_\_\_\_ zero(s) on $(1,8]$.

Place each of the digits 5, 6, 7, and 8 in exactly one square to make the smallest possible sum. What is this sum? [asy]draw((0,.5)--(10,.5),linewidth(1));
draw((4,1)--(6,1)--(6,3)--(4,3)--(4,1),linewidth(1));
draw((7,1)--(9,1)--(9,3)--(7,3)--(7,1),linewidth(1));
draw((7,4)--(9,4)--(9,6)--(7,6)--(7,4),linewidth(1));
draw((4,4)--(6,4)--(6,6)--(4,6)--(4,4),linewidth(1));
