\begin{tabular}{r}
$P 7 R$ \\
$+\quad 39 R$ \\
\hline$R Q 0$
\end{tabular}

Given the function $f(x) = m - |x-1| - |x-2|$, where $m \in \mathbb{R}$, and the solution set of $f(x+1) \geq 0$ is $[0, 1]$.  
(1) Find the value of $m$;  
(2) If $a, b, c, x, y, z \in \mathbb{R}$, and $x^2 + y^2 + z^2 = a^2 + b^2 + c^2 = m$, prove that $ax + by + cz \leq 1$.

Milton spilled some ink on his homework paper again. He can't read the coefficient of \(x^2\), but he knows that the equation has two distinct negative, integer solutions. What is the sum of all of the distinct possible integers that could be under the ink stain?

[asy]
draw((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle);
fill((0,0)--(3,0)--(3,3)--(0,3)--cycle,black);
label("$x+25=0$",(3,1.5),E);
label("$x^{2}+$",(0,1.5),W);
[/asy]

In a magic square, the sum of the three entries in any row, column, or diagonal is the same value. The square below shows four of the entries of a magic square. Find $x$.
[asy]
size(2cm);
for (int i=0; i<=3; ++i) draw((i,0)--(i,3)^^(0,i)--(3,i));
label("$x$",(0.5,2.5));label("$25$",(1.5,2.5));
label("$75$",(2.5,2.5));label("$5$",(0.5,1.5));
[/asy]

