2. Solve the quadratic equation $x(x-2)=x-2$;
3. Simplify and evaluate $(x+2+\frac{4}{x-2})÷\frac{x^{3}}{x^{2}-4x+4}$, where $x$ is a suitable non-negative integer that satisfies $x\leqslant 2$.

Sets $C$ and $D$, shown in the Venn diagram, are such that the total number of elements in set $C$ is three times the total number of elements in set $D$. Altogether, there are 4500 elements in the union of $C$ and $D$, and their intersection has 1200 elements. What is the total number of elements in set $C$?

[asy]
label("$C$", (2,67));
label("$D$", (80,67));
draw(Circle((30,45), 22));
draw(Circle((58, 45), 22));
label("1200", (44, 45));
[/asy]

